# First Notes on String 1 (repertoire plan: st-first-notes-string-1). An original study in C
# major on the thinnest string: the open string 1 (E), fret 1 (F) with finger 1, fret 3 (G) with
# finger 3. Steps everywhere except one skip, E up to G in bar 5. The teacher strums C and G7, one
# chord a bar; every note belongs to the chord under it or passes by step (F between E and G, E
# between two Fs). It ends on E over C.
